post_install() {
	cat <<'EOF'
polystrata: run `polystrata` to set up and start the server.

The first run compiles the engine for your GPU (10-40 minutes) and downloads
the model files (tens of GB) into ~/PolyStrata (override with the
POLYSTRATA_HOME environment variable). Later runs just start the server.

  polystrata            set up if needed, then start the model
  polystrata --help     upstream setup options (model, context, GPU, ...)
  polystrata-update     rebuild the engine and refresh the Python packages
                        without starting the model

NVIDIA: install the `cuda` package first (upstream builds with CUDA 13.0).
AMD: a system ROCm 7 in /opt/rocm is used when present, otherwise ROCm is
downloaded into the venv on the first start. See /opt/polystrata/docs/.
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
	post_install
}
